 bypassing passlib entirely.\n\n**New endpoints added (`/auth/` router):**\n- `POST /auth/register` \u2014 creates user, returns access + refresh token pair\n- `POST /auth/login` \u2014 OAuth2 password form, returns both tokens  \n- `POST /auth/refresh` \u2014 accepts refresh token, issues new pair\n- `GET /auth/me` \u2014 returns caller's user info\n\n**Token security:**\n- Access tokens: 15-minute expiry, `type: \"access\"`\n- Refresh tokens: 7-day expiry, `type: \"refresh\"`\n- Refresh tokens are rejected on protected endpoints (enforced via `type` claim)\n\n**All 32 tests pass**, including 12 new tests covering registration, login, refresh flow, and the security invariant that refresh tokens can't authenticate API routes.", "\u2713 Done  ($1.2793)"], "done": true}